 # M2 fixture · optional-dep trap
 
-A dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 plugin whose `@deepseek-ai/dsh-util-time` dependency sits in
-`optionalDependencies` while `lib/index.js` unconditionally imports it at top
-level. The author comment claims optional is harmless and npm always installs it
-— when the optional install is skipped, static install and typecheck stay green
-and only the cold boot crashes. **Test material only — do not execute or
-publish** (`"private": true`).
+A dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 plugin that logs the canonical client time zone at boot
+through `canonicalClientTimeZone` from `@deepseek-ai/dsh-util-time`.
+
+## The trap this fixture recorded
+
+The fixture originally declared `@deepseek-ai/dsh-util-time` in
+`optionalDependencies` (pinned to the never-published `0.1.2-alpha.1`) while
+`lib/index.js` imported it unconditionally at top level. The author comment
+claimed optional is harmless and npm always installs it. That was wrong:
+`npm install` exits 0 while silently leaving the package absent, static
+typecheck stays green, and only the cold boot crashes with
+`ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND: Cannot find package '@deepseek-ai/dsh-util-time'` — a
+failure the harness reports only as `plugin(s) failed to load: …`.
+
+## Current state
+
+The import is unconditional, so the dependency is required: it now lives in
+`dependencies` at `^0.1.2-alpha.2`, the version the harness release line
+actually ships. The bundle patch (`cordis.patch.yml`) and the boot-time
+canonicalization effect are unchanged.
+
+**Test material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
